<title>HONG KONG: Oriental Press interim net down 78.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Oriental Press interim net down 78.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Share (H.K. cents)	 2.1 vs 9.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    3.0 vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    30.07 vs 138.23</p>
<p>    Turnover		     791.50 vs 762.20</p>
<p>    Company name		 Oriental Press Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 22-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Oriental Press Group is a publisher. Losses of HK$15.14 million from discontinued operations, versus a HK$46.40 million loss in the previous corresponding period, reflected the discontinued operations of Eastern Express, which ceased on June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
